3,Macaguaje language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/macaguaje_language,"Macaguaje (also spelled Makaguaje; ISO 639-3: mcl) is a dormant Western Tucanoan language of the Colombian Amazon, spoken by the Makaguaje people in the foothills of the department of Caquetá, particularly in the community of Teófila Arenosa in the municipality of Solano. [1]",Macaguaje,Tucanoan
